{"actor":{"id":"claude-opus-4-8","type":"agent"},"content":{"blocks":[{"caller":{"type":"direct"},"id":"toolu_01SwADR4dNwz2JnCYWCCTetZ","input":{"content":"# WIP technical design\n\n**Status:** exploratory impressions, nothing locked in — including the\nimplementation language. This records how the problem looks after building\nconversation-ledger and turnbridge, so later work does not start cold.\n\n## Inputs\n\nThe only required input is Conversation Ledger. Events are read through its\nlibrary API (`readEvents`, `sortEvents`) or `cledger export`, grouped by\n`conversation.id`. Everything needed to derive first-class edges is already\npresent:\n\n- `conversation.id` / `seq` — node identity and intra-conversation order.\n- `links` (e.g. `{rel:\"continues\", target}`) — turnbridge's `continuation`\n  lineage edges, and any future `supersession` links.\n- `actor.id` — author, for same-author edges.\n- `context.repo` / `branch` / `head` / `cwd` — repository grounding and, later,\n  the join key to code/doc nodes.\n- `occurred_at` — temporal adjacency.\n- content blocks — file paths mentioned in tool calls (`Read`, `Edit`, `Bash`),\n  which yield conversation→file edges once file nodes exist.\n\n## Node and edge model (draft)\n\n**Nodes** are conversations to start with: `{id, repo, author, first/last\nactivity, turn_count, title}`, referencing the ledger rather than copying\ncontent. The model is deliberately widened from day one so conversations are a\n*subgraph* of an eventual repo-wide graph — a node carries a `type`\n(`conversation` now; `file`, `commit`, `decision` later) and a stable\n`normalized_identifier`.\n\n**Edges** are typed and evidence-bearing: `{src, dst, kind, basis:[event_ids],\nconfidence}`. Candidate kinds:\n\n- `continuation` — from turnbridge `links`; explicit, high confidence.\n- `supersession` — a later decision overriding an earlier one (explicit when\n  linked; otherwise a candidate for intent-recall, not this tool, to assert).\n- `shared_file` — two conversations touched the same path.\n- `same_author` / `temporal_adjacency` — weak, co-occurrence edges; kept\n  clearly lower-confidence so they are not mistaken for explicit links.\n- `reference` — a conversation names another conversation/commit/file.\n\nExplicit edges (from `links`) are authoritative; derived edges (co-occurrence)\nalways carry their basis and a confidence so a consumer can filter.\n\n## Downstream target: tagseq2tagseq\n\ntagseq2tagseq trains on a **text-attributed document graph**. Its extractor\nlayer is three protocols — `ContentSource` (iterate `Document{identifier,\nnormalized_identifier, content, metadata}`), `LinkExtractor` (raw link targets\nfrom content), `LinkNormalizer` (canonical ids) — feeding a `GraphBuilder` that\nwrites `graph.jsonl`, one node per line with `outgoing`/`incoming` edge sets,\n`char_count`, and `metadata`, which the model then traverses (e.g. random\nwalk).\n\nThis tool should emit exactly that shape, so the conversation graph drops into\ntagseq2tagseq as a new `source_type`:\n\n- a conversation node → a `Document` whose `content` is its rendered transcript\n  (reuse turnbridge's literal-transcript renderer) and whose `normalized_id`\n  is the ledger `conversation.id`;\n- typed edges collapse into `outgoing`/`incoming` for training, but the richer\n  `{kind, basis, confidence}` is retained in `metadata` so nothing is lost;\n- alternatively, implement the conversation graph *as* a tagseq2tagseq\n  `ContentSource`+`LinkExtractor` pair rather than re-emitting JSONL. Which side\n  owns the adapter is open.\n\n## Generalization to a whole-repo graph\n\nThe larger ambition — graph every cross-file connection (code imports, doc\nlinks, conversation↔file, commit↔decision) — is the same `GraphBuilder` with\nmore extractors: one `ContentSource`/`LinkExtractor` per content type, sharing\none identifier namespace so a conversation node and the file it discusses are\njoinable. The conversation extractor is just the first. Keeping node identity\nand edge shape uniform now is what lets that compose later instead of forcing a\nrebuild. Whether the repo-wide graph lives here or in a later sibling is\nundecided; the design assumes it should be able to.\n\n## Open questions\n\n- **Language.** Reads TS (conversation-ledger) and feeds Python\n  (tagseq2tagseq). Emit neutral `graph.jsonl` from TS, or implement as a Python\n  tagseq2tagseq extractor, or split. Undecided.\n- **Storage.** Recompute the graph on demand (pure index) vs. persist it (and\n  if persisted, in git notes like the ledger, or a separate artifact).\n- **Cross-repo / cross-user.** The ledger can hold synced conversations from\n  collaborators; does the graph span repos, and how are identifiers namespaced\n  across them.\n- **Edge derivation ownership.** Which derived edges belong here vs. are left to\n  intent-recall to assert with its confidence machinery, to avoid two tools\n  claiming the same relationship differently.\n- **Rebuild determinism.** Guaranteeing the same events produce byte-identical\n  `graph.jsonl` (stable node/edge ordering) so the graph is diffable and\n  cacheable.\n","file_path":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/conversation-graph/docs/WIP_TECHNICAL_DESIGN.md"},"name":"Write","type":"tool_use"}],"role":"assistant"},"context":{"branch":"main","cwd":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/turnbridge","head":"49da723e6046dbccfcf0e3966f6e68a44a5964dd","repo":"git@github.com:evintunador/turnbridge.git"},"conversation":{"id":"claude-code:c158a677-efd7-4ff4-87ac-1c3052566c2e","seq":844},"id":"ev1-a5647937f88202c9cf37f93e0a833948885964e85a5ad76642492219d0b9087e","kind":"conversation_turn","occurred_at":"2026-07-19T17:17:13.708Z","producer":{"session_id":"c158a677-efd7-4ff4-87ac-1c3052566c2e","source":"claude-code","tool":"cledger","version":"0.2.0"},"raw":{"data":{"cwd":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/turnbridge","effort":"high","entrypoint":"cli","gitBranch":"main","isSidechain":false,"message":