upersedes an earlier decision, several that touch the\nsame files) into explicit, addressable edges. Its first consumer is a human\nasking \"how does this discussion relate to that one?\"; its second is a training\npipeline that traverses the graph.\n\nThis repository is intentionally at the design stage. Nothing here is locked\nin — it records current impressions and the shape of the problem, not a\ncommitted API. See [product intent](docs/PRODUCT_INTENT.md) and the\n[WIP technical design](docs/WIP_TECHNICAL_DESIGN.md).\n\n## Where it sits\n\n- **conversation-ledger** — neutral, immutable store of conversation events\n  (the source of truth this tool reads).\n- **turnbridge** — captures/moves conversations between CLIs; already writes\n  `continuation` lineage edges into the ledger that this tool would surface.\n- **intent-recall** — reads the ledger to answer \"what was intended?\"; a\n  sibling consumer, not a dependency.\n- **conversation-graph** (this repo) — reads the ledger, emits an explicit\n  relationship graph.\n- **[tagseq2tagseq](https://github.com/evintunador/tagseq2tagseq)** — trains\n  language models by traversing a text-attributed document graph; a natural\n  downstream consumer of the graph this tool emits (see the design doc).\n\n## License\n\n[MIT](LICENSE)\n","filePath":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/conversation-graph/README.md","originalFile":null,"structuredPatch":[],"type":"create","userModified":false},"type":"user","userType":"external","uuid":"6d816c14-8c0e-40b4-864f-b1b934a8697a","version":"2.1.215"},"format":"claude-code-jsonl/1"},"recorded_at":"2026-07-19T17:18:00.107Z","schema":"conversation-ledger/v1"}
{"actor":{"type":"human"},"content":{"blocks":[{"content":"File created successfully at: /Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/conversation-graph/docs/PRODUCT_INTENT.md (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)","tool_use_id":"toolu_01QNxb3AzTPEMGSdYfuH7AfX","type":"tool_result"}],"role":"user"},"context":{"branch":"main","cwd":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/turnbridge","head":"49da723e6046dbccfcf0e3966f6e68a44a5964dd","repo":"git@github.com:evintunador/turnbridge.git"},"conversation":{"id":"claude-code:c158a677-efd7-4ff4-87ac-1c3052566c2e","seq":841},"id":"ev1-be391f248717e6171f0cef7cf87a311565ba9ace5a32aead2e23d073a7b1a1db","kind":"conversation_turn","occurred_at":"2026-07-19T17:16:39.524Z","producer":{"session_id":"c158a677-efd7-4ff4-87ac-1c3052566c2e","source":"claude-code","tool":"cledger","version":"0.2.0"},"raw":{"data":{"cwd":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/turnbridge","entrypoint":"cli","gitBranch":"main","isSidechain":false,"message":{"content":[{"content":"File created successfully at: /Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/conversation-graph/docs/PRODUCT_INTENT.md (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)","tool_use_id":"toolu_01QNxb3AzTPEMGSdYfuH7AfX","type":"tool_result"}],"role":"user"},"parentUuid":"cc7280b5-8886-426e-abb8-a2fde0edac85","promptId":"5802adfd-dd29-4252-b8b0-ed28762a2d6d","sessionId":"c158a677-efd7-4ff4-87ac-1c3052566c2e","session_id":"c158a677-efd7-4ff4-87ac-1c3052566c2e","slug":"generic-stirring-candy","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"cc7280b5-8886-426e-abb8-a2fde0edac85","timestamp":"2026-07-19T17:16:39.524Z","toolUseResult":{"content":"# Product intent\n\n**Status:** design-stage impressions. Nothing here is committed; it exists to\nframe the problem and record early opinions, and is expected to shift.\n\n## Purpose\n\nConversation Graph makes the relationships *between* conversations explicit and\naddressable. Conversation Ledger stores conversations as immutable events with\nenough provenance to reconstruct each one, but the connections among them —\nthis conversation continues that one in another CLI, this decision supersedes\nan earlier one, these three all edited the same file — live only implicitly in\ntimestamps, `links`, and shared context. This tool reads the ledger and\nproduces an explicit graph of those relationships that both a human and a\nmachine can traverse.\n\n## Behavioral commitments (intended)\n\n- Derive edges from evidence already in the ledger; never invent a relationship\n  the record does not support.\n- Keep every edge traceable back to the event(s) that justify it — a graph is a\n  derived view, and the raw record stays authoritative.\n- Treat the graph as rebuildable: it is an index over the ledger, not a second\n  source of truth, and re-deriving it from the same events yields the same\n  graph.\n- Distinguish edge *kinds* (continuation, supersession, shared-file,\n  same-author, temporal-adjacency, reference) rather than flattening everything\n  into one \"related\" link.\n- Make edge confidence and its basis visible, so a weak co-occurrence edge is\n  not mistaken for an explicit continuation.\n\n## Non-goals (for now)\n\n- Deciding which conversation is \"correct\" or ranking intent — that is\n  intent-recall's job; this tool supplies structure, not judgment.\n- Capturing conversations or moving them between CLIs — that is turnbridge.\n- Becoming a second store: the graph holds references and derived edges, not\n  copies of conversation content.\n\n## Relationship to the other tools\n\nConversation Graph is a **reader** of Conversation Ledger, a peer of\nintent-recall (both derive views from the ledger; neither depends on the\nother), and a **producer** for downstream consumers — most concretely\n[tagseq2tagseq](https://github.com/evintunador/tagseq2tagseq), whose training\npipeline traverses a text-attributed document graph. turnbridge already emits\n`continuation` lineage edges into the ledger; this tool is the first that reads\nthem as graph structure rather than as per-row labels.\n\n## The bigger idea (not this tool yet)\n\nThe same machinery generalizes past conversations to *every cross-file\nconnection in a repository* — code importing code, docs linking docs, a\nconversation that discusses a file, a commit that implements a decision — as\none heterogeneous graph. Whether that lives here or in a later sibling is\nundecided. It is called out in the technical design because it shapes the node\nand edge model even at this stage: the conversation graph should be a subgraph\nof that larger graph, not a differently-shaped thing that has to be rebuilt.\n","filePath":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/conversation-graph/docs/PRODUCT_INTENT.md","originalFile":null,"structuredPatch":[],"type":"create","userModified":false},"type":"user","userType":"external","uuid":"df9c6650-edd3-402d-bc64-8f843ea02da5","version":"2.1.215"},"format":"claude-code-jsonl/1"},"recorded_at":"2026-07-19T17:18:00.107Z","schema":"conversation-ledger/v1"}
